      "writtenOn": "2021-07-20T11:17:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Even then I think it\u0027s very confusing. Writing to disk is strictly unnecessary because the stats will be read back from memory anyway, not from disk. The only thing you\u0027re after here is the syncStats() method, which is super confusingly named as what it does is wait for the worker to finish processing the enqueued tasks.\n\nHow about :\n\n  Upon calling \"cmd battery unplug\" a task is scheduled on the battery\n  stats worker thread. Because network battery stats are only recorded\n  when the device is on battery, this test needs to wait until the\n  battery status is recorded because causing traffic. \n  Writing stats to disk is unnecessary, but --write waits for the worker\n  thread to finish processing the enqueued tasks as a side effect. This\n  side effect is the point of using --write here.\n\nI guess ideally BatteryStatsService would have a command to wait, instead of having to use this method which looks related but is in fact unrelated. But now is not really the time to do that.",
      "parentUuid": "de2cff81_3145716b",
